(7084138, 1077201, 34171, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dennisheckman:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a brilliant star trails image. I have taken a few night shots with stars, but have not tried to do trails yet. Maybe you can post your technique later? bumping. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!   This was my first attempt at star trails as well.  I had shot one shot prior to this one with the same settings, but at 1600iso and it was way blown out, so I dialed it back to 200iso and left it open for another 2hrs.  In PS I boosted the saturation quite a bit and that was all.</td>', 'Originally posted by Dennisheckman: This is a brilliant star trails image. I have taken a few night shots with stars, but have not tried to do trails yet. Maybe you can post your technique later? bumping.   Thank you!   This was my first attempt at star trails as well.  I had shot one shot prior to this one with the same settings, but at 1600iso and it was way blown out, so I dialed it back to 200iso and left it open for another 2hrs.  In PS I boosted the saturation quite a bit and that was all.', '2013-08-08 14:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7084140, 1077678, 161988, '<td valign="top">Stunning Karen!</td>', 'Stunning Karen!', '2013-08-08 14:08:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7084141, 1077335, 161988, '<td valign="top">Perfect camera angle and timing for this shot.  You also put right down on the ground where the rodeo clown would be. Have the view from his perspective.  Can''t ask for more!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-08-08 13:15:22.</i></td>', 'Perfect camera angle and timing for this shot.  You also put right down on the ground where the rodeo clown would be. Have the view from his perspective.  Can''t ask for more!', '2013-08-08 14:14:47.000000', '2013-08-08 14:15:22.000000', 0),
(7084142, 1077606, 161988, '<td valign="top">There was just so much competition amongst the top finishers in this challenge that it made ribboning difficult cause this is brilliant. Obviously the bird in the background hurt your chances but I presume rules didn''t allow you to edit it out.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-08-08 13:18:27.</i></td>', 'There was just so much competition amongst the top finishers in this challenge that it made ribboning difficult cause this is brilliant. Obviously the bird in the background hurt your chances but I presume rules didn''t allow you to edit it out.', '2013-08-08 14:17:05.000000', '2013-08-08 14:18:27.000000', 0),
(7084143, 1077606, 17203, '<td valign="top">We used Bold Coast Charters out of Cutler Harbor. They''re pretty much the only choice for Machias Seal Island unless you depart from Canada. The advantage of Bold Coast is that you have the opportunity (conditions permitting) of going ashore on the nesting island and shooting from blinds, which is an entirely different experience from most puffin tours operating from boats. You have to make reservations by April at the latest to secure a spot in June-August.</td>', 'We used Bold Coast Charters out of Cutler Harbor. They''re pretty much the only choice for Machias Seal Island unless you depart from Canada. The advantage of Bold Coast is that you have the opportunity (conditions permitting) of going ashore on the nesting island and shooting from blinds, which is an entirely different experience from most puffin tours operating from boats. You have to make reservations by April at the latest to secure a spot in June-August.', '2013-08-08 14:18:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7084144, 1077606, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Trotterjay:</b></div><hr/><i>Obviously the bird in the background hurt your chances but I presume rules didn''t allow you to edit it out. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Of course I would have preferred the foreground bird alone. I had many other puffin photos that were better for composition, etc. but it was just such an amusing pose that I went with this one. My second choice wasn''t a puffin at all and probably would have ribboned. I''ll save that one for Best of 2013.</td>', 'Originally posted by Trotterjay:Obviously the bird in the background hurt your chances but I presume rules didn''t allow you to edit it out.  Of course I would have preferred the foreground bird alone. I had many other puffin photos that were better for composition, etc. but it was just such an amusing pose that I went with this one. My second choice wasn''t a puffin at all and probably would have ribboned. I''ll save that one for Best of 2013.', '2013-08-08 14:22:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7084154, 1076736, 62357, '<td valign="top">this is wonderful</td>', 'this is wonderful', '2013-08-08 15:07:50.000000', NULL, 0),
